Suggests: dislocker, exfatprogs
Description: repair Windows boot entry and Windows health from Linux
 winbootfix repairs two common Windows problems from a Linux system:
  - the "Windows Boot Manager" UEFI entry disappeared and the PC no longer
    starts Windows (NVRAM entry, EFI boot files, BCD store);
  - Windows starts but works badly: graphics driver not loaded, DLL files of
    the wrong architecture or damaged, damaged system files.
 .
 It only diagnoses by default, backs everything up before any change and
 schedules a post-repair script that runs at the next Windows sign-in.
